# stemLM needs no environment variables to build, test or run locally.
#
# `.env` and `.env.*` are gitignored (except this file): keep local-only values there and never
# commit them. Everything compiled into the extension is readable by anyone who installs it, so a
# secret must never reach an extension build.
#
# Usage analytics (src/lib/analytics.ts) sends events only from a build that has this key AND is
# installed from a store. Put the PostHog *project* API key (phc_..., designed to be public) in
# `.env.production.local`, which only `wxt build` and `wxt zip` read. Without it, nothing is sent.
# A PostHog *personal* API key is a secret and must never appear here or in the bundle.
#
# WXT_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_...
